/*Q1. Write a Java program to implement a basic calculator using a class mechanism. The program should include the following:
Aclass named Calculator with the following methods:
• add(int a, int b): Returns the sum of two integers.
• subtract(int a, int b): Returns the difference of two integers.
• multiply(int a, int b): Returns the product of two integers.
• divide(int a, int b): Returns the result of dividing two integers as a double. If the divisor is zero, display a message: "error division"
and return 0.0.
Input Format:
• The first line contains an integer representing the first number.
• The second line contains an integer representing the second number.
Output Format:
• Print the results of the operations as follows:
Addition: <result>
Subtraction: <result>
Multiplication: <result>
Division: <result>
or
error division //If division by zero occurs
Note:
• The result of the division should be formatted to 2 decimals.
• Returning 0.0 is required for handling inside the program, but should not be printed as output
*/
import java.util.Scanner;
 
class Calculator {
    int add(int a, int b) { return a + b; }
    int subtract(int a, int b) { return a - b; }
    int multiply(int a, int b) { return a * b; }
 
    double divide(int a, int b) {
        if (b == 0) {
            System.out.println("error division");
            return 0.0;                      // returned, but not printed
        }
        return (double) a / b;
    }
}
 
public class CalculatorDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        int a = sc.nextInt();
        int b = sc.nextInt();
        Calculator calc = new Calculator();
        System.out.println("Addition: " + calc.add(a, b));
        System.out.println("Subtraction: " + calc.subtract(a, b));
        System.out.println("Multiplication: " + calc.multiply(a, b));
        if (b != 0) {
            System.out.printf("Division: %.2f%n", calc.divide(a, b));
        } else {
            calc.divide(a, b);               // prints "error division"
        }
        sc.close();
    }
}
